An interface declaring one exported method whose every implementation carries a
body with no statement, which is the marker shape. One function takes the
interface as a parameter type and calls the method through neither implementation.

-- go.mod --
module example.com/app

go 1.27.0
-- main.go --
package main

// Sealed is implemented by declaring the marker method.
type Sealed interface {
	Sealed()
}

type one struct{}

func (one) Sealed() {}

type two struct{}

func (two) Sealed() {}

func present(s Sealed) bool { return s != nil }

func main() { println(present(one{}), present(two{})) }
